% Option 'coatedpaper': use the versions of the colors intended for coated paper
%
% UiT's 2019 graphic profile specifies two sets of CMYK values for each of its
% colors: "bestrøket" (coated) and "ubestrøket" (uncoated). This has to do with
% the target paper: glossy or not. My understanding is that most regular office
% paper is uncoated, so that is the default. The graphic designers making
% glossy brochures will probably not be using LaTeX, but if they are, they can
% specify the CMYK color mode (`\selectcolormode{cmyk}`) and load this package
% with the `coatedpaper` option.
% [UiTs fargepalett]: https://uit.no/ansatte/grafiskprofil#innhold_617372
\newif\if@uit@coated\@uit@coatedfalse
\DeclareOption{coatedpaper}{\@uit@coatedtrue}

\ProcessOptions\relax

